  "text" : "One number to open with.\nThis is what a real breech costs priced live right now by our own engine, thirty four thousand nine hundred and fifty eight pounds, not a red or green dot.\nA number you can actually act on.\nHere's the idea, and it's now built.\nGovernance isn't a checkbox pass or fail.\nIt's a priced, versioned, continuously retuned judgment.\nThe whole chain from risk appetite to enforcement to evidence treated like a software dependency, signed, pinned, updated by reviewed pull request.\nEvery other team is still arguing about frameworks.\nWe just built the thing running and honest about what isn't, and I mean built, not Slidware.\nThis is the real terminal three Kubernetes clusters live right now.\nDriftwood, Ludlow, Tuppence, up nineteen days, each reconciling from a signed Git source on its own with nobody watching, seven hundred and thirty two files, twenty nine independent verify scripts, nothing here stands in for a thing that doesn't work."
